## Why This Is Asked

Tests ownership, bias-for-action, and customer-obsession in a privacy-risk incident requiring cross-functional coordination and rapid containment.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-functional incident response and escalation
- Tenant-scoped controls and safe toggles without data loss
- Privacy, auditability, and regulatory implications
- Clear customer and leadership communication; postmortems and preventive controls

## Code Example

```javascript
// Tenant-scoped feature flag sample
const featureEnabledForTenant = isFeatureEnabledForTenant(tenantId);
if (featureEnabledForTenant) {
  runFeature();
} else {
  skipFeature();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate no new cross-tenant exposures after patch?
- What metrics would you use to measure long-term risk reduction?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to take ownership under time pressure, address bias ethically, and balance customer impact with product experimentation.

## Key Concepts

- Ownership and accountability in cross-functional triage
- Bias detection, containment, and mitigation in live features
- Trade-off reasoning between hotfix vs rollback vs pausing experiments
- Customer communications and leadership updates without leaking internal data

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: simple bias-mitigating ranking patch
function mitigateBias(ranking, sensitiveFeature) {
  const w = ranking.weights;
  if (sensitiveFeature.confidence > 0.8) {
    w[sensitiveFeature.name] *= 0.75;
  }
  return computeScore(ranking);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the patch across languages and locales?
- What metrics indicate sustained bias reduction after deployment?
